1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,650
Coney Island, Before It Was a Nature Park

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:07,224
Coney Island in New York
had a switchback railway,

3
00:00:07,304 --> 00:00:11,250
a Ferris wheel and a million
visitors on a hot Sunday.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:14,460
Coney Island in Singapore
has a locked gate,

5
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:19,625
a gravel track and a sign asking
cyclists to slow down for wildlife.

6
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:23,358
The name travelled here in
1950, attached to a small

7
00:00:23,438 --> 00:00:26,731
island off Punggol that
a businessman had just

8
00:00:26,811 --> 00:00:30,550
bought and meant to turn
into a seaside playground.

9
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:34,825
That plan failed, as did the
ones before and after it.

10
00:00:34,825 --> 00:00:38,558
What finally opened to the
public in 2015 was close

11
00:00:38,638 --> 00:00:42,525
to the opposite of a resort,
and that was the point.

12
00:00:42,525 --> 00:00:45,479
The island's older name
is Pulau Serangoon,

13
00:00:45,559 --> 00:00:49,571
and for most of its history
it was a thin, wooded strip of

14
00:00:49,651 --> 00:00:53,250
land off the Punggol coast
with nothing much on it.

15
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:58,075
That changed in 1937, when
Aw Boon Haw bought it.

16
00:00:58,075 --> 00:01:02,389
He and his brother Aw Boon Par
had built the Tiger Balm fortune,

17
00:01:02,469 --> 00:01:05,685
and Aw Boon Haw put a
beach villa on the island:

18
00:01:05,765 --> 00:01:09,461
a single-storey house of
about 600 square metres in the

19
00:01:09,541 --> 00:01:12,551
modern style of the day,
with a central hall,

20
00:01:12,631 --> 00:01:17,300
an open verandah running around it
and its own well for fresh water.

21
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:21,399
The design is usually attributed
to Ho Kwong Yew, one of the

22
00:01:21,479 --> 00:01:26,075
architects then bringing a plainer,
flat-roofed look to Singapore.

23
00:01:26,075 --> 00:01:28,746
Locals stopped calling the place Pulau

24
00:01:28,826 --> 00:01:32,300
Serangoon and started
calling it Haw Par Island.

25
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:35,750
The villa did not last long as a retreat.

26
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:41,641
The Japanese Occupation damaged it along
with much of the Aw family's property,

27
00:01:41,721 --> 00:01:45,425
and after the war Aw Boon
Haw sold the island on.

28
00:01:45,425 --> 00:01:48,191
The buyer, in 1950, was a local

29
00:01:48,271 --> 00:01:51,300
businessman named Ghulam Mahmood.

30
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:55,597
He paid around $100,000 and
announced that he would remake the

31
00:01:55,677 --> 00:01:59,621
island as a holiday resort
for ordinary working families:

32
00:01:59,701 --> 00:02:03,856
swimming, boating and fishing,
a skating rink, a dance hall,

33
00:02:03,936 --> 00:02:08,525
a restaurant and bar, and a handful
of cottages for honeymooners.

34
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:13,120
He renamed it Coney Island, after
the New York amusement district,

35
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:17,450
and advertised it as Singapore's
first island health resort.

36
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:21,147
For a while it ran, with
launches crossing every half

37
00:02:21,227 --> 00:02:25,075
hour and a house band billed
as the Coney Island Band.

38
00:02:25,075 --> 00:02:26,900
It did not take.

39
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:31,025
Within about three years the
island was up for auction.

40
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:34,859
A succession of owners followed,
none of whom found a way

41
00:02:34,939 --> 00:02:38,704
to make the resort idea work,
and by the early 1970s the

42
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:42,962
island belonged to a businessman
from Thailand who was trying,

43
00:02:43,042 --> 00:02:46,475
without success, to sell
it for a million dollars.

44
00:02:46,475 --> 00:02:49,945
A group of us went out to the island once

45
00:02:50,025 --> 00:02:53,575
during our national service, around 1979.

46
00:02:53,575 --> 00:02:56,759
It was well before any of this was a park,

47
00:02:56,839 --> 00:02:59,325
or even a name most people knew.

48
00:02:59,325 --> 00:03:03,805
The place was overgrown and
completely quiet, with a low building

49
00:03:03,885 --> 00:03:08,025
coming apart among the trees
and a beach full of driftwood.

50
00:03:08,025 --> 00:03:12,450
Nobody stopped us, because there
was nobody there to stop us.

51
00:03:12,450 --> 00:03:17,125
The government acquired
Coney Island in 1972.

52
00:03:17,125 --> 00:03:20,987
Two years later the Port of
Singapore Authority began

53
00:03:21,067 --> 00:03:24,557
a reclamation project
costing about $20 million,

54
00:03:24,638 --> 00:03:28,128
which enlarged the small
original island several

55
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:32,150
times over and built a bridge
across to the mainland.

56
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:36,574
A second round of filling came in
the 1990s, this time as part of

57
00:03:36,654 --> 00:03:42,186
Punggol new town, and it closed most of
the water between the island and Punggol,

58
00:03:42,266 --> 00:03:45,800
leaving a channel only
about a hundred metres wide.

59
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:49,946
There had been a proposal in
the 1980s to close that last

60
00:03:50,026 --> 00:03:54,400
gap as well and fold the island
into the mainland outright.

61
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:58,027
It was dropped after objections
that joining it on would

62
00:03:58,107 --> 00:04:01,550
take away the very thing
that made it worth keeping.

63
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:05,675
For most of these decades
the island was simply shut.

64
00:04:05,675 --> 00:04:08,721
It was fenced off,
absent from the bus map,

65
00:04:08,801 --> 00:04:12,000
used for grazing cattle
and for little else.

66
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,366
Coney Island Park opened on
the 10th of October 2015,

67
00:04:16,446 --> 00:04:20,975
run by the National Parks
Board, at about 50 hectares.

68
00:04:20,975 --> 00:04:24,075
The design is deliberately spare.

69
00:04:24,075 --> 00:04:26,766
There are five short stretches of beach,

70
00:04:26,846 --> 00:04:31,338
labelled A to E, a gravel spine a
little over two kilometres long,

71
00:04:31,418 --> 00:04:34,050
and boardwalks over the wetter ground.

72
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:37,473
There is almost nothing to
buy, the toilets compost

73
00:04:37,553 --> 00:04:40,850
rather than flush, and
the lighting is kept low.

74
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:44,162
Much of the tree cover
is casuarina, some of it

75
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:47,049
self-sown from seed carried in by birds,

76
00:04:47,129 --> 00:04:51,675
and about eighty bird species
have been recorded on the island.

77
00:04:51,675 --> 00:04:54,610
In the park's first year
a single Brahman bull,

78
00:04:54,690 --> 00:04:58,715
thought to be a leftover from the
cattle that once grazed there,

79
00:04:58,795 --> 00:05:02,900
wandered the tracks and drew a
small following of photographers.

80
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:06,476
It died in October 2016,
during a health check,

81
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:09,664
and the BBC gave it an obituary headlined

82
00:05:09,744 --> 00:05:13,400
"the life and death of
a lonely Singapore cow."

83
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,918
The Haw Par villa is still standing,

84
00:05:15,998 --> 00:05:20,400
roofless and fenced off, back
among the trees near the shore.

85
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:24,825
The otters, the wild pigs and
the birds arrived on their own.

86
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,425
The irony is not hidden.

87
00:05:27,425 --> 00:05:30,708
For sixty years people
tried to sell this island

88
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:33,651
as somewhere to have fun, as a beach club,

89
00:05:33,731 --> 00:05:37,375
a fairground, a honeymoon
spot, and none of it held.

90
00:05:37,375 --> 00:05:40,889
The version that finally
worked is the one that asks

91
00:05:40,969 --> 00:05:44,425
nothing of visitors and
sells them nothing at all.

92
00:05:44,425 --> 00:05:48,539
Where it fits in the bigger
story: A fair amount of what looks

93
00:05:48,619 --> 00:05:52,475
like leftover nature in
Singapore is nothing of the kind.

94
00:05:52,475 --> 00:05:57,620
Coney Island is larger than it was born,
tied to the shore by reclaimed land,

95
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:01,216
planted up, and presented
as wilderness in large part

96
00:06:01,296 --> 00:06:05,775
because the earlier and more
commercial ideas for it fell through.

97
00:06:05,775 --> 00:06:09,825
The rough edges are a
decision, not an accident.
